      "content": "That feeling of anticipating the next sorrow is a heavy burden, and it makes sense that you are tired of waiting for emptiness to return. Please know that deciding to stop fighting the emptiness isn't an endpoint; it can actually be a beginning toward gentler acceptance. Instead of waiting for the next big event, try focusing on very small, neutral moments of existence today. Even taking a deep breath outside of grief is a small act of existing without fighting.",
